nese-student-studying-in-canada-arrested-by-us-authorities-for-espionage-like-activities-sister-says-if-my-brother-is-a-chinese-spy-then-i-am-trumps-father/articleshow/133775016.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-05T00:11:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133775379,imgsize-63580.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1989, Detroit Zoo began saving lost snails; 37 years later, 500 head 5,000 miles to Tahiti]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133754476.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Hundreds of tiny snails are journeying over 5,000 miles from Michigan to Tahiti. This release is part of a long-running international conservation program for endangered native snails. Invasive predators had caused severe population collapses for these unique mollusks in their native islands. The Detroit Zoo has been breeding and caring for these snails since 1989. This ongoing effort has successfully returned over 17,000 snails to their natural habitat.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1989-detroit-zoo-began-helping-save-snails-wiped-out-in-the-wild-37-years-later-500-are-travelling-5000-miles-to-tahiti-part-of-a-program-that-has-returned-17000/articleshow/133754476.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1989-detroit-zoo-began-helping-save-snails-wiped-out-in-the-wild-37-years-later-500-are-travelling-5000-miles-to-tahiti-part-of-a-program-that-has-returned-17000/articleshow/133754476.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-05T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133754756,imgsize-2223574.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gold miners breached 14 hectares of Indonesia's orangutan refuge in three years; conservationists want government to intervene]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133752652.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Jantho forest reservation in Indonesia, vital for orangutan rehabilitation, is under siege from illegal gold miners. This encroachment places the habitat of critically endangered Sumatran orangutans, rescued from illegal trade, at severe risk. Mining activities have already destroyed approximately fourteen hectares, while toxic runoff threatens the surrounding Krueng Aceh River, endangering both community health and wildlife.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/gold-miners-have-breached-a-refuge-built-for-rescued-orangutans-14-hectares-of-indonesias-sanctuary-damaged-in-3-years/articleshow/133752652.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/gold-miners-have-breached-a-refuge-built-for-rescued-orangutans-14-hectares-of-indonesias-sanctuary-damaged-in-3-years/articleshow/133752652.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-05T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133752764,imgsize-102930.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma veteran restores 400-acre ranch as native grasses and streams return]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133752086.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-oklahoma-a-veteran-spent-5-years-fighting-back-invasive-cedars-on-his-400-acre-ranch-now-native-grasses-are-returning-and-water-is-flowing-into-newly-reappearing-streams/articleshow/133752086.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-oklahoma-a-veteran-spent-5-years-fighting-back-invasive-cedars-on-his-400-acre-ranch-now-native-grasses-are-returning-and-water-is-flowing-into-newly-reappearing-streams/articleshow/133752086.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-05T00:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133752128,imgsize-568412.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California oil field faces $20 million funding gap in 25-year fight to stop development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133732212.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[West Coyote Hills, a 510-acre former oil field in Fullerton, California, has faced development pressure for five decades. After 25 years of efforts to preserve the land, a plan is now close to completion. California has approved a $95 million purchase of the remaining site, with $75 million already committed. Supporters are seeking the final $20 million to permanently protect the habitat as parkland and a nature preserve.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-former-california-oil-field-has-faced-development-pressure-for-50-years-after-a-25-year-preservation-fight-supporters-are-20-million-short-of-a-95-million-land-purchase/articleshow/133732212.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-former-california-oil-field-has-faced-development-pressure-for-50-years-after-a-25-year-preservation-fight-supporters-are-20-million-short-of-a-95-million-land-purchase/articleshow/133732212.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-05T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133733449,imgsize-169390.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1978, New York advocates sought affordable homes; nearly 50 years later, 145-home community is complete]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133734484.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After more than four decades of hurdles, a housing initiative from Long Island, initiated in 1978, has finally come to fruition with 145 affordable homes at Matinecock Court. This $98 million project overcame extensive legal and political challenges since its inception, which is linked to a pivotal Fair Housing Act case that reached the Supreme Court.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1978-advocates-sought-affordable-homes-in-a-new-york-town-nearly-50-years-and-a-landmark-court-battle-later-a-98-million-community-with-145-homes-is-finally-complete/articleshow/133734484.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1978-advocates-sought-affordable-homes-in-a-new-york-town-nearly-50-years-and-a-landmark-court-battle-later-a-98-million-community-with-145-homes-is-finally-complete/articleshow/133734484.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T23:55:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133734816,imgsize-2359855.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Arnold Schwarzenegger: "Never follow the crowd, go where it's…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133773229.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-arnold-schwarzenegger-never-follow-the-crowd-go-where-its-a-powerful-advice-on-success/articleshow/133773229.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-arnold-schwarzenegger-never-follow-the-crowd-go-where-its-a-powerful-advice-on-success/articleshow/133773229.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T23:31:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133774134,imgsize-89704.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Chile community harvests up to 650,000 litres of water yearly from coastal fog]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133772318.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/this-chilean-community-catches-fog-in-giant-nets-and-turns-coastal-mist-into-water-the-unusual-idea-now-harvests-up-to-650000-litres-a-year-in-a-drought-hit-region/articleshow/133772318.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/this-chilean-community-catches-fog-in-giant-nets-and-turns-coastal-mist-into-water-the-unusual-idea-now-harvests-up-to-650000-litres-a-year-in-a-drought-hit-region/articleshow/133772318.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T23:20:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133773514,imgsize-1410361.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2002, South Australia sank ex-HMAS Hobart in under 3 minutes; 18 years later...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133767550.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Having been decommissioned and sunk in 2002, the ex-HMAS Hobart has evolved into a lively underwater ecosystem. This former Australian warship is now home to more than fifty distinct fish species, while its submerged structure nurtures an array of filter-feeding organisms. Located in a safeguarded marine park sanctuary, it offers an enticing destination for divers eager to explore successful efforts in habitat rehabilitation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2002-south-australia-sank-ex-hmas-hobart-in-under-3-minutes-18-years-later-a-marine-survey-recorded-more-than-50-fish-species-around-the-destroyer/articleshow/133767550.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2002-south-australia-sank-ex-hmas-hobart-in-under-3-minutes-18-years-later-a-marine-survey-recorded-more-than-50-fish-species-around-the-destroyer/articleshow/133767550.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T22:53:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133772695,imgsize-1054520.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Billionaire heiress Isabel Getty, great-granddaughter of J. Paul Getty, marries Faris McKinnon]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133770894.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Billionaire dynasty heiress Isabel Getty, great-granddaughter of oil tycoon J. Paul Getty, has married British financier Faris McKinnon in an intimate London ceremony. The couple exchanged vows at Chelsea Old Town Hall before celebrating at Harry’s Bar in Mayfair. Isabel and Faris later made a stylish exit in a vintage black Rolls-Royce, accompanied by their young son Viggo.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/billionaire-heiress-isabel-getty-great-granddaughter-of-oil-tycoon-j-paul-getty-marries-british-financier-faris-mckinnon-in-intimate-london-wedding-newlyweds-make-grand-exit-in-vintage-rolls-royce/articleshow/133770894.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/billionaire-heiress-isabel-getty-great-granddaughter-of-oil-tycoon-j-paul-getty-marries-british-financier-faris-mckinnon-in-intimate-london-wedding-newlyweds-make-grand-exit-in-vintage-rolls-royce/articleshow/133770894.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T22:26:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133771199,imgsize-166295.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia’s endangered eastern quolls welcome new joeys; after vanishing from mainland for 60 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133731245.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Australia’s endangered eastern quolls are showing signs of recovery after conservationists successfully bred captive-raised animals in Tasmania. One released female has six joeys in her pouch, offering hope for the species’ future. Eastern quolls disappeared from mainland Australia by the 1960s, largely due to habitat loss, disease, road accidents and predation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australias-endangered-eastern-quolls-have-welcomed-new-joeys-after-vanishing-from-the-mainland-for-60-years-the-species-is-now-breeding-again-in-a-rare-conservation-comeback/articleshow/133731245.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australias-endangered-eastern-quolls-have-welcomed-new-joeys-after-vanishing-from-the-mainland-for-60-years-the-species-is-now-breeding-again-in-a-rare-conservation-comeback/articleshow/133731245.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T22:23:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133731989,imgsize-122186.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ricky Hatton’s mansion, where he was found dead in 2025, sold for £1.5m, £350k below asking price]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133768975.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Late boxing legend Ricky Hatton’s luxury mansion in Greater Manchester has sold for £1.5 million, £350,000 below its original asking price. The five-bedroom property, where Hatton was found dead in 2025, featured a heated indoor pool, jacuzzi, gym, cinema, games room and Manchester City memorabilia. The sale comes amid reports over his estate.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ricky-hattons-luxury-mansion-where-the-boxing-legend-was-found-dead-in-2025-sold-for-1-5-million-350000-below-original-asking-price-five-bedroom-home-featured-pool-gym-and-manchester-city-memorabilia/articleshow/133768975.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/ricky-hattons-luxury-mansion-where-the-boxing-legend-was-found-dead-in-2025-sold-for-1-5-million-350000-below-original-asking-price-five-bedroom-home-featured-pool-gym-and-manchester-city-memorabilia/articleshow/133768975.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T21:15:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133769072,imgsize-183120.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA["You guys were the issue": FaZe Banks drops explosive truth about FaZe Clan’s end]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133759488.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[During a recent livestream, FaZe Banks candidly discussed the challenges facing FaZe Clan, pinpointing former members like Stable Ronaldo as key contributors to its decline. He revealed an astonishing eleven million dollar investment in creators that yielded no profits, questioning Ronaldo's financial ou